    description "The two books, The Passing of the Great Race (1916), and The Rising Tide of Color Against White Supremacy (1921) are making tremendous inroads into the thinking of American citizens who are frightened by the racial makeup of America due to the huge and fast paced racial demographic shifts taking place in the country. The distinguished panel led by Dr. Douglas Foster, will help us see how this material written over 100 years ago is being used today to fuel the resurgence of White Supremacy, Christian Nationalism, and the Great Replacement Theory. They explore how this dangerous ideology may be seducing Christians to succumb to its powerful influence."
